---
import Site from '../layouts/Site.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import MarketRiskLadder from '../components/MarketRiskLadder';
import '../styles/g13-sidepages.css';
import { release, url } from '../lib/publication';
const claim = (id: string) => release.claims.find(c => c.id === id);
const source = (id: string) => {
  const item = claim(id);
  return item ? url(`/sources/${item.evidenceIds[0]}/`) : url('/sources/');
};
const rain = claim('C-IMD-RAINFALL-DEP-india-20260923');
const premises = claim('C-NSO-PREMISES-2018');
const sufficiency = claim('C-NSO-SUFFICIENCY-2018');
const functionSurvey = claim('C-JJM-FUNCTIONALITY-2024');
const karnataka = claim('C-KA-DROUGHT-ORDER-20260922');
const foodBudget = claim('C-NSO-HCES-FOODSHARE-202324');
const onion = claim('C-DCA-ONION-BLR-YOY-20260923');
const jswRisk = claim('C-JSW-WATER-RISK-202526');
const jswPrior = claim('C-JSW-NO-MATERIAL-WATER-INCIDENT-202425');
const ceaWater = claim('C-CEA-RAW-WATER-LOSS-201617');
---
<Site title="The cost is not in the rain gauge" description="An evidence-led account of potential effects on livelihoods and unequal water access, with dated surveys and no invented 2026 loss total.">
  <PageHeader title="The cost is not in the rain gauge" eyebrow="People / livelihoods / unequal access" description="Rainfall describes weather. The human story needs records of crops, work, prices, service and the time people spend finding water." />
  <section class="section g11-chapter"><div class="shell"><div class="g11-chapter-head"><span class="g11-chapter-number">01</span><div><p class="eyebrow">The line we cannot yet cross</p><h2>A deficit is not a loss estimate.</h2></div></div>
    <div class="grid-2"><p class="g11-pull"><span class="g11-tag measured">Measured · IMD reported</span><br />India's rainfall was <strong>−14.9%</strong> against the normal for 1 June–23 September 2026. <a href={rain ? source(rain.id) : url('/sources/')}>Source and dates ↗</a></p><div class="g11-clock"><p>That graphic cannot count failed harvests, lost wages, tanker spending, illness or migration. We have no approved 2026 series that establishes those outcomes or a national total. It would be wrong to multiply one rainfall percentage into an economic loss.</p></div></div>
  </div></section>
  {onion && <section class="section g11-chapter"><div class="shell"><div class="g11-chapter-head"><span class="g11-chapter-number">02</span><div><p class="eyebrow">One observed market signal / two dates</p><h2>A price moved. Its cause is still a question.</h2></div></div><p class="g11-pull">At one Department of Consumer Affairs monitored Bengaluru centre, its reported onion price rose by ₹34/kg between the same calendar date in 2025 and 2026. That change cannot be assigned to rainfall from this record.</p><div class="g13-price-stage"><p class="eyebrow">DCA centrewise retail reports · Bengaluru / onion / ₹ per kg</p><div class="g13-price-grid"><div class="g13-price-value"><span>23 September 2025</span><strong>₹23</strong><small><a href={url('/sources/E-DCA-ONION-BLR-20250923/')}>Original DCA report for this date ↗</a></small></div><div class="g13-price-value"><span>23 September 2026</span><strong>₹57</strong><small><a href={url('/sources/E-DCA-ONION-BLR-20260923/')}>Original DCA report for this date ↗</a></small></div></div><p>+₹34/kg · +147.8% from the displayed earlier price</p><p class="small">Two discrete monitored values, not a continuous series or a Bengaluru city average. The centre report does not state the sample volume or reason for the change. <a href={source(onion.id)}>Claim, selection method and limits ↗</a></p></div></div></section>}
  {rain && jswRisk && jswPrior && ceaWater && <div class="shell" id="markets"><MarketRiskLadder client:load reviewedAsOf="24 September 2026" physical={{headline:'India rainfall was 14.9% below its normal for those dates.',place:'India / broad national reading',observationPeriod:'1 June–23 September 2026',description:'IMD reported 713.3 mm received against 837.7 mm normal. This is the physical context for a water-risk question, not a plant-specific source reading.',limitation:'The published national total cannot be assigned to JSW Steel facilities, their water sources or their operating outcomes.',sources:[{label:'IMD rainfall record',href:source(rain.id),claimId:rain.id}]}} exposure={{company:'JSW Steel',reportingPeriod:'FY2025–26 risk report',headline:'Non-availability of water is a disclosed production risk.',description:'The company says it is developing reservoirs near facilities and pursuing efficiency and site-specific zero-liquid-discharge measures.',limitation:'A company risk disclosure and mitigation plan do not show that a 2026 monsoon-linked interruption occurred.',sources:[{label:'JSW risk disclosure',href:source(jswRisk.id),claimId:jswRisk.id}]}} historicalCea={{fiscalYear:'FY2016–17',outages:24,potentialGenerationLossMu:2875.79,denominatorNote:'CEA reports this as 0.18% of maximum possible generation for the reviewed thermal units.',source:{label:'CEA historical performance review',href:source(ceaWater.id),claimId:ceaWater.id}}} /><div class="g11-clock"><span class="g11-tag history">Company self-report · FY2024–25</span><h3>A risk can exist without a recorded material loss.</h3><p>JSW Steel said no water-related incident had <em>materially</em> affected its costs or revenues over the preceding four fiscal years. That is the company's thresholded historical statement, not proof of no smaller incidents or a verdict on this later monsoon. <a href={source(jswPrior.id)}>Company report and limits ↗</a></p></div></div>}
  <section class="section g11-chapter"><div class="shell"><div class="g11-chapter-head"><span class="g11-chapter-number">03</span><div><p class="eyebrow">Different starting points</p><h2>Access was uneven before this season.</h2></div></div>
    <div class="g11-signal-grid">{premises && <article class="g11-signal"><span class="g11-tag measured">Measured · 2018 survey</span><span>Rural households</span><strong>58.2%</strong><p>reported a drinking-water facility within their premises. This is not a 2026 tap-service measure.</p><a href={source(premises.id)}>NSO survey ↗</a></article>}{premises && <article class="g11-signal"><span class="g11-tag measured">Measured · 2018 survey</span><span>Urban households</span><strong>80.7%</strong><p>reported a facility within their premises under the same survey definition.</p><a href={source(premises.id)}>NSO survey ↗</a></article>}{functionSurvey && <article class="g11-signal"><span class="g11-tag measured">Measured · 2024 sample</span><span>Already-covered villages</span><strong>86.5%</strong><p>of surveyed households with taps had received water in the preceding seven days. This sample is not all rural India.</p><a href={source(functionSurvey.id)}>Functionality assessment ↗</a></article>}</div>
    {sufficiency && <p class="small muted">In the same 2018 NSO survey, 87.6% of rural and 90.9% of urban households said their principal source supplied sufficient water throughout the year. That is self-reported sufficiency, not a 2026 quality test or daily service log. <a href={source(sufficiency.id)}>Survey record ↗</a></p>}
    <p class="g11-pull">Those are three distinct measurements, not one improving or worsening time series.</p>
  </div></section>
  <section class="section g11-chapter"><div class="shell"><div class="g11-chapter-head"><span class="g11-chapter-number">04</span><div><p class="eyebrow">Where harm would appear</p><h2>Follow the consequence, then ask for the record.</h2></div></div>
    <div class="grid-3"><article class="g11-branch"><p class="eyebrow">Farms and food</p><h3>From rain to harvest is not a straight line.</h3><p>Which crop, at which stage, on irrigated or rainfed land? A claim of damage needs dated sowing, yield or crop-survey evidence in that place, plus other possible causes. <a href={karnataka ? source(karnataka.id) : url('/sources/')}>Karnataka's order</a> directs a survey; its result is not approved here.</p><a href={url('/response/')}>See the declaration stage ↗</a></article><article class="g11-branch"><p class="eyebrow">Work and prices</p><h3>Trace a disruption before pricing it.</h3><p>The Bengaluru onion centre's two reported prices are real snapshots, but the cause is not in the report. Check named supply, production and trade records before attributing a price move. No water-caused 2026 loss or inflation total is published here.</p><a href={onion ? source(onion.id) : url('/journalists/')}>Inspect this price comparison ↗</a></article><article class="g11-branch"><p class="eyebrow">Households</p><h3>A pipe, a schedule, a safe sample.</h3><p>Which households bought or used storage, pumps, treatment or purchased water in a named place this season, and at what cost? Did shared pipes or sources constrain even those who could pay? Dated service records and interviews are needed before describing a 2026 coping pattern.</p><a href={url('/water-and-people/')}>Understand access ↗</a></article></div>
    {foodBudget && <div class="g11-clock"><span class="g11-tag history">Historical budget context · NSO 2023–24</span><h3>Why food prices would matter to household budgets</h3><p>Food made up <strong>47.04%</strong> of average rural and <strong>39.68%</strong> of average urban monthly per-person expenditure in NSO's 2023–24 survey, excluding imputation of selected free government-provided items. These are national rural/urban averages, not the shares for low-income households. They do not establish a 2026 food-price rise or any water-linked household loss. <a href={source(foodBudget.id)}>Survey factsheet and denominator ↗</a></p></div>}
  </div></section>
  <section class="section g11-chapter"><div class="shell"><div class="g11-chapter-head"><span class="g11-chapter-number">05</span><div><p class="eyebrow">What would change this page</p><h2>Show impact, and show recovery.</h2></div></div><p>For each named place, match weather and source records to delivered service, crop results, prices and household experience on the same dates. Publish the denominator, who was observed, what changed and alternative explanations. Track restoration too: a repaired scheme or replenished source matters only when its outcome is measured.</p><div class="g11-epilogue"><p class="eyebrow">The current verdict</p><h3>Exposure is plausible. Realized 2026 losses are not verified here.</h3><p>That gap is a reporting assignment, not reassurance that no one has been harmed.</p><div class="button-row"><a class="button" href={url('/states/')}>Start with a place ↗</a><a class="button button-light" href={url('/data-status/')}>See missing evidence ↗</a></div></div></div></section>
</Site>
